# MLB pitcher workload and arm-injury study (improved version)
#
# Improvements built in:
#   1. Starters and relievers are analyzed separately.
#   2. Workload spikes: recent 7/14-day pitches vs the 28-day norm, plus change vs the prior 28 days.
#   3. Injury history: previous arm injured-list placements.
#   4. Age and season workload (pitches so far this season, last season's total).
#   5. Matched controls (risk-set design): every injured pitcher is compared with healthy pitchers
#      of the same role, who pitched on the SAME date and are closest in age.
#   6. Mixed-effects model (random intercept per pitcher) plus a matched-set (conditional) logistic model.
#   7. Validation on other seasons: train on two seasons, test on the third.
#
# Setup:   pip install pybaseball pandas numpy requests scipy scikit-learn statsmodels
# Run:     put this file in the SAME project folder as your earlier script (the one that created the
#          "mlb_data" folder). It reuses the saved Statcast weeks, so it does not re-download pitches.
# Output:  files in mlb_data/study_results/  (open summary.txt first)

